From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:12:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Preserve PME endpoint wake policy when adding WAKE# GPIO

PCI PM marks PME-capable devices as wakeup-capable without enabling
system wakeup. Configuring a WAKE# GPIO subsequently enables system
wakeup unconditionally. A PME-capable WLAN endpoint can then assert
WAKE# during system suspend even when its driver has configured no
WoWLAN triggers.

For PME-capable endpoints, keep the wakeup policy initialized by PCI PM
when attaching the dedicated GPIO IRQ. The PM core arms it when the
endpoint is allowed to wake the system. Keep default activation on
bridges and on devices whose GPIO adds the wakeup capability.

Codex traced PCI enumeration and PM wake IRQ setup and drafted the
change. Validation covers Linux 7.3.3 patch replay and the ARM64 PCI OF
object under the Piano configuration.

Fixes: 071e245ab749 ("PCI: Add support for PCIe WAKE# interrupt")
Link: https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/+/071e245ab749c52338ec4eb7fe0a9bb2cee97492
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/pci/of.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/of.c b/drivers/pci/of.c
index a51dff91b..53c969bfe 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/of.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/of.c
@@ -628,7 +628,13 @@ static void pci_configure_wake_irq(struct pci_dev *pdev, struct gpio_desc *wake)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	device_init_wakeup(&pdev->dev, true);
+	/*
+	 * pci_pm_init() already set the wakeup capability for endpoints
+	 * that support PME. Registering an additional wake signal must
+	 * preserve their system wakeup policy.
+	 */
+	if (pci_is_bridge(pdev) || !pdev->pme_support)
+		device_init_wakeup(&pdev->dev, true);
 }
 
 void pci_configure_of_wake_gpio(struct pci_dev *dev)
